Abstract = {This paper discusses the potential of force perception technologies for
   realizing hand-held devices in the field of social systems. We introduce
   an interactive system based on force perception technology called ``Come
   Over Here, or Catch You!{''}, which is a force-sensation-based
   navigation system for waiters. It consists of our new hand-held haptic
   interface which can provide perceptually continuous and translational
   force, and a position and posture identification system. Since the
   proposed compact haptic interface does not require an external ground it
   can be used outside the laboratory and does not interrupt human
   behavior. We verify the feasibility of the system in trials.},
