Note = {2nd International Conference on Advanced Science and Information
   Technology (ASCIT), Cheonan, SOUTH KOREA, MAY 12-13, 2017},
Abstract = {This study was attempted to reduce the recurrence rate by using multiple
   regression analysis to identify stress, stress coping strategies and
   self-management factors that may affect tuberculosis. The data were
   collected from 110 patients who were admitted to the tuberculosis
   hospital in M city. Data were analyzed by multiple regression using SAS
   program. The results showed that stress perception, stress coping,
   problem centered coping, and emotional centered coping had a significant
   effect on self-management. Also, as the stress perception was low and
   problem centered coping strategies were used more frequently, the
   self-management performance score increased and the recurrence rate
   could be reduced.},
