   American Health Care Exchanges-GMEPE/PAHCE, Mexicali, MEXICO, APR 07-11,
   2025},
Organization = {Institute of Electrical and Electronics Engineers Inc},
Abstract = {The visual system enables us to perceive our environment and perform
   functions such as safe navigation. An example of a critical component of
   effective perception is gaze stability, which relies on the vestibular
   system. The vestibular system is also essential for the perception and
   control of self-movement. This study explores the behavior of cortical
   areas associated with these systems, examining differences in
   hemodynamic responses under conditions when visual attention is present
   versus when is absent, using tNIRS to assess brain activity. The
   experiment involved 19 participants, allowing for a clear distinction
   between these two conditions. The results revealed specific cortical
   areas exhibiting different patterns of activity during task performance.},
