Note = {22nd Congress of the International Ergonomics Association-IEA, SOUTH
   KOREA, AUG 25-29, 2024},
Abstract = {The integration of Yi ethnic graphics with contemporary artistic styles
   has emerged as a significant area of study. However, current research
   tends to focus on traditional art forms or general modern design
   techniques, overlooking the fusion of these distinct areas. This study
   seeks to evaluate the efficacy of layout design guidelines that
   incorporate the concept of visual flow. Thirty participants took part in
   an eye-tracking experiment, where eight pairs of images were tested
   following the guidelines outlined in a graphic design book. The findings
   revealed that only one pair of images aligned with the guideline.
   Notably, various graphic components, including figures, faces, and
   background images, significantly influenced visual flow. This conclusion
   underscores the importance of designers considering the complex
   interplay between attention-grabbing elements and visual strategies that
   may regulate viewers' gazing behavior.},
