   (INTECOL), FLORENCE, ITALY, JUL 19-25, 1998},
Organization = {Soc Human Ecol; Japanese \& Italian Soc Human Ecol},
Abstract = {The population, economic development, natural resources and environment
   of Nepal have been analysed. The annual population growth rate of 2.6\%
   is very high; the urban growth rate is the highest in South Asia,
   despite Nepal's current position as the least urbanised country in the
   region. Life expectancy is 55 years for men and 52 years for women:
   Nepal is one of only three countries in the world where female life
   expectancy is lower than for males. The maternal mortality rate, like
   the infant mortality rate and under five mortality rate, is very high.
   The incidence of water- and waste-related diseases is common in Nepal
   (44\% of all child deaths). Illiteracy amounts to 65\% of the adult
   population with 82\% of females illiterate. The human development
   indices have been calculated with the most recent data available: of the
   160 countries covered by the index, Nepal is in 131st position.
   The problems existing in Nepal are serious and, therefore, management of
   natural resources in the area is urgently needed to check further
   degradation and to meet the growing demands of the population. An
   ecosystem approach has been proposed for water resource conservation and
   an environmentally sustainable development of Nepal.},
