   Thuyloi Univ, Hanoi, VIETNAM, SEP 25-28, 2019},
Organization = {NAFOSTED; LONG THANH; FECON; LICOGI 16; SHENLIAN},
Abstract = {In order to fully utilize the freshwater and improve urban water
   environment, the feasibility studies of tidal sluice construction have
   been carried out in recent years. The key problem is sediment siltation
   at the reach downstream the gate. Based on measured data of
   sedimentation under existing tidal sluices of estuaries, this paper
   analyzes characteristics and strength of siltation downstream tidal
   sluices in different regions of China, and evaluates sedimentation of
   tidal sluices according to reduction of river cross section, reduction
   of discharge capacity and watercourse length downstream tidal sluices;
   analyzes overall sediment deposition of watercourse downstream tidal
   sluices, sediment deposition and sediment thickness of some river
   reaches. The analysis shows that the longer the watercourse downstream
   tidal sluices, the greater the total volume of sediment deposition;
   annual average sediment deposition in each kilometer is 40 similar to
   186,000 m(3) according to overall sedimentation of watercourse
   downstream tidal sluices; back-silting intensity is the largest within
   the first year after tidal sluice built, annual sediment thickness is
   about 1.1m, decreases gradually and tends to be stable. Width of
   watercourse downstream tidal sluices involved in this paper are among
   100 similar to 250m and influence of watercourse width on sediment
   deposition needs to be further analyzed.},
