Organization = {Intelligent Informat Technol Applicat Res Assoc; Indt Geodesy \&
   Geophys; Chinese Acad Sci; Engn Technol Press},
Abstract = {With the rapid development of urbanization and the rapid development of
   information technologies, the amount of valuable data captured in
   different systems and different structures grew and technical progress
   made it possible to exchange and share data by these different systems
   and different structures. Urban information is a kind of multi-sources
   data, which not only contains spatial data, but also contains
   non-spatial data. These information have the characteristic of multiple
   types, multiple scales, large data, different data formats etc. The
   variety of these data demands that the data integration system could
   read all types of data, frame uniform standard to classify these data,
   establish the data relationship among them and integrate usable data
   resource. In search of solutions for these problems, the paper discusses
   how to design the frame of the urbanization system and how to manage and
   store multi-sources data. The paper implements the data integration
   system in the environment of NET combined of GDAL/OGR library and ArcGIS
   Engine. In this paper, data are stored into the database in the form of
   a binary and metadata table are constructed to manage the multi-sources
   data. Application proves that the design of system and data management
   in the system is feasible, and something useful is concluded.},
