   Sludge by HEDTA and Oxalic Acid},
Booktitle = {PROGRESS IN ENVIRONMENTAL SCIENCE AND TECHNOLOGY, VOL III: PROCEEDINGS
   OF THE 2011 INTERNATIONAL SYMPOSIUM ON ENVIRONMENTAL SCIENCE AND
   TECHNOLOGY},
Year = {2011},
Pages = {1010-1015},
Note = {3rd International Symposium on Environmental Science and Technology
   (2011 ISEST), Dongguan, PEOPLES R CHINA, JUN 01-04, 2011},
Organization = {Chinese Soc Environm Sci; Beijing Inst Technol; Amer Chem Soc, ENVR Div;
   Beijing Inst Technol, State Key Lab Explos Sci \& Technol; Dongguan Sci
   \& Technol Museum},
Abstract = {Ultrasound and microwave were applied to enhance extraction of heavy
   metals in sewage sludge with oxalic acid and hydroxyethyl
   ethylenediamine triacetic acids (HEDTA), and the effects of radiation
   time, power and energy of ultrasound and microwave on the extraction of
   heavy metals from sewage sludge were investigated. Besides, species of
   heavy metals fractions in sewage sludge before and after extraction were
   analyzed by the application of Tessier's sequential extraction
   procedure. In general, the extracted fractions of Cu, Ni and Cr in
   sludge were improved with the increase of time, power and energy, the
   extracted fraction of Zn had not been obviously improved. After the
   ultrasonic-assisted and microwave chemical extraction, the contents of
   organic compounds and residue forms of Cu, Cr and Ni were decreased.
   However, the contents of exchangeable and carbonate compounds forms were
   slightly increased, the speciation of Zn in sludge was hardly changed.},
