Note = {2nd International Conference on Energy and Environment Technology,
   Changsha, PEOPLES R CHINA, DEC 04-06, 2010},
Abstract = {The permanent magnet EDS train has been considered to be one of the most
   promising urban transportation vehicles due to its particular
   characteristics: simple configurations, low energy consumption, low
   noise, and suitable for high speed conditions. In order to study the
   characteristics of permanent magnet Electrodynamic Suspension ( EDS)
   system, an experimental mechanism was established in this paper. The
   optimization of Halbach magnet array has been carried out and
   appropriate track for the EDS experimental mechanism has been
   established. The characteristics of the permanent-magnet EDS system have
   been achieved by static and dynamic experiments. As a conclusion, the
   permanent magnet EDS system is appropriate to apply on high speed field.
   Moreover, experiments validate that some damping should be introduced
   into the system to obtain better stability performance because the EDS
   system is inherently instable.},
