Organization = {Malaysia Tech Scientist Assoc},
Abstract = {Ciamis Regency is one of many regencies in West Java province,
   Indonesia, which has a lot of tourism destinations. But unfortunately,
   after 2012, tourist arrivals to Ciamis regency was dropped dramatically.
   The aim of this study is to investigate the tourists' satisfaction
   levels about tourism destination attributes in Ciamis Regency. The
   questionnaires were distributed to 400 respondents and the
   Importance-Performance Analysis (IPA) was then employed to map the
   tourist's satisfaction attributes into the IPA diagram. The results of
   this study show that there are six attributes that lie in quadrant A.
   These attributes need to be a priority to improve because they are
   considered important by the respondents but still has low-performance
   perception. These attributes are: The Availability of Directions,
   Destination Information on the Internet, Cleanliness, Clear and Complete
   Information About the Tourism Destination, Environmental Conservation
   and Culinary Attractiveness. Other six attributes lie in quadrant B
   (high expectations and high-performance perceptions), so then these
   attributes should be maintained to keep the tourist satisfaction. Other
   12 attributes lie in Quadrant C (low expectations and low-performance
   perceptions) and quadrant D. Since the tourists give only slight
   expectations to them, then these attributes may give less priority
   improve.},
