   JAPANESE NEURAL NETWORK SOCIETY - PROCEEDINGS, VOLS 1-3},
Year = {1998},
Pages = {869-872},
Note = {5th International Conference on Neural Information Processing (ICONIP
   98) / 1998 Annual Conference of the Japanese-Neural-Network-Society
   (JNNS 98), KITAKYUSHU, JAPAN, OCT 21-23, 1998},
Organization = {Japanese Neural Network Soc; Asian Pacific Neural Network Assembly},
Abstract = {This paper presents an approach that self-develops the grasping ability
   in a robot without external supervision. The robot has human-like
   structure used for hand-eye coordination, and the self-development is
   implemented based on observation in developmental psychology: human
   babies gradually become to grasp a target along their growing through
   actively interacting with environment. Via a learn-by-doing manner, the
   grasping operation is obtained by learning of mapping between
   non-retinal (motion) information of the vision and the arm motion. It is
   considered that retinal information processing such as visual size
   perception is also obtained simultaneously. Visual size perception is
   used to make preshape of the hand possible prior to final object grasp.},
