   Antalya, TURKEY, APR 22-25, 2010},
Abstract = {This study looked at the emotional reaction, behaviour, appearance and
   trauma experienced by incest victims. Subjects were 10 female victims of
   incest. The data collected was based on semi-structured interviews and
   observations. The process of transcription and analysing the interviews
   was conducted using content analysis. Three category of emotions shown
   by the victims were sadness, stable and absence of grief. Behaviors
   shown were passive and stable. Victims appearance were properly dressed
   with hair neatly combed. Two victims were acted rough and masculin. A
   total of five victims suffered trauma due to repeated nightmares and
   three victims attempted suicide. (C) 2010 Elsevier Ltd. All rights
   reserved.},
