   of therapy because they often represent the expression of human
   tensions, problems or conflict. The therapy is relying on projective
   identification processes, bringing the unconscious at the surface, in a
   controlled way during therapy sessions, so the client can experience
   catharsis, releasing all the negative emotions. Our study aims to
   achieve a meta-analysis of the existing assesments used in art therapy
