Abstract = {Aim of this study is to find out whether personality profiles predispose
   pain severity of patients with Tension Type Headache (TTH). The
   Cross-sectional study was used by performing consecutive sampling method
   towards 67 respondents from TTH Clinic of Neurology Outpatient Unit of
   Dr. Soetomo General Hospital, Surabaya. Instruments : Visual Analog
   Scale (VAS) and Minnesota Multiphasic Personality Inventory-2 (MMPI-2).
   Result : Most respondents suffered from chronic TTH. Mean VAS Score was
   5.608 +/- 1.8765 (5.1236-6.0931, CI 95\%) cm. RC7 was statistically
   significant with VAS Score than others (p=0.013). People with
   predisposition to experience dysfunctional negative emotion particularly
   anxiety, demonstrate to have higher pain severity},
