Abstract = {We present a review of regulatory atmospheric dispersion models and
   their application to environmental impact assessment (EIA) in Finland.
   The following regulatory models are available: the urban dispersion
   modelling system, models for dispersion of vehicular pollution, the air
   pollution information system, and the dispersion model for odorous
   compounds. All of these models are connected to a meteorological
   pre-processing model, based on atmospheric boundary-layer scaling. We
   will also discuss the application of these models in EIA, and the
   research needs for model development in general.},
