Note = {Conference on Gender and Sexualities - Revisioning Drug and Alcohol
   Research, Aarhuus Univ, Aarhus, DENMARK, OCT 12, 2012},
Organization = {Ctr Alcohol \& Drug Res},
Abstract = {The paper develops key notions needed for a feminist embodiment approach
   to drugs, their use and users. First, the term embodied deviance is
   defined in relationship to women drug users. Second, the bodily tasks of
   gendered drug use are defined to show how ``normal{''} embodiment is
   foreclosed to women drug users. Third, disease regimes and
   epistemologies of ignorance are introduced. Fourth, another piece is
   inserted into the feminist embodiment puzzle emotions. Simply, we look
   at some of the practices that emerge from the affective dimensions of
   gendered drug use. In the concluding section of my paper, I ask, ``Where
   do we go from here?{''}},
